      "message": "WDYT about just looking up the infos here instead of keeping a `std::vector\u003cstd::weak_ptr\u003cbool\u003e\u003e` and several `std::shared_ptr\u003cbool\u003e`  throughout the info structs? IIUC, we only need to know validity at the time of snapshot saving.\n\n```\nbool AreDescriptorDependenciesStillValid(const DescriptorSetInfo::DescriptorWrite\u0026 \n write) {\n   switch (write.writeType) {\n     case BUFFER: {\n       return mBufferInfo.find(write.bufferInfo.buffer) !\u003d mBufferInfo.end();\n     }\n     ...\n     default:\n       ERR();\n   }\n }\n ```\n \nThis helps to keep the info structs a little more simple and avoids lots of small allocations and atomics for the `std::shared_ptr` handling during normal operation time and instead just adds the small cost of a couple hashmap lookups at snapshot time.",
